472 - A Song of Heaven and Homeland
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 472
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[F]Sometimes I hear strange music,
[F7]Like [Bb]none e’er heard be[F]fore,
Come [C]floating softly [F]earthward
As [G7]thro’ heav’n’s open [C7]door:
It [F]seems like angel voices,
[F7]In [Bb]strains of and [F]love,
That swell the [Bb]mighty [F]chorus
[Bb]A[F]round the [C7]throne a[F]bove.
O [A]sweet, celestial [Dm]music,
[F]Heard [C]from a [C7]land a[F]far-
The song of Heav’n and Homeland,
[Bdim7]Thro’ [F]doors God [C7]leaves a[F]jar!

Refrain:
[F]O sweet, celestial music,
[F7]Heard [Bb]from a [F]land afar-
[C]The song of [F]Heav'n and Homeland,
[G7]Thro' doors [C7]God leaves ajar!

Verse 2:
[F]Now soft, and low, and restful,
[F7]It floods [Bb]my soul [F]with peace,
[C]As if [F]God's benediction
[G7]Bade all [C7]earth's troubles cease.
[F]Then grander than the voices,
[F7]Of wind, [Bb]and wave, [F]and sea-
[Bb]It fills the [F]dome of heaven
[Bb][F]With [C7]glorious [F]harmony.

Verse 3:
[F]This music haunts me ever,
[F7]Like [Bb]something heard [F]in dreams-
[C]It seems to [F]catch the cadence
[G7]Of heav'nly [C7]winds and streams,
[F]My heart is filled with rapture,
[F7]To think, [Bb]some day [F]to come,
[Bb]I'll sing it [F]with the angels-
[Bb]The [F]song of [C7]heav'n [F]and home.
